Description: Compare folded string bytes independently of plain char signedness
 qstricmp and qstrnicmp subtract char values after ASCII case folding. UTF-8
 bytes therefore sort before ASCII on signed-char targets and after ASCII on
 unsigned-char targets. This changes generated HTML search indexes between
 amd64 and arm64. Compare both folded bytes as unsigned, as strcmp does.
Author: Qore Technologies, s.r.o.
Forwarded: no
